# Example S3 Storage Configuration for Staging/Production
# Copy this and fill in your actual AWS credentials for staging/production deployments

# Storage driver - use 's3' for cloud storage
STORAGE_DRIVER=s3

# AWS S3 Configuration
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_BUCKET=hostelstagingbucket
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIA4DWIA7WTY6PLHCNA
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=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

# Alternative: Use environment-specific buckets
# Staging:
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=hostelstagingbucket
# 
# Production:
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=hostelproductionbucket

# Generated image URL format:
# https://<bucket>.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/hostels/<hostelId>/full/<file>.webp

# Notes:
# 1. Create an IAM user with S3 permissions:
#    - s3:PutObject (upload)
#    - s3:DeleteObject (delete)
#    - s3:GetObject (optional, for serving via CloudFront)
#
# 2. For better security, consider:
#    - Using IAM roles (if in EC2/ECS)
#    - Using AWS SigV4 signing
#    - Enabling bucket versioning
#    - Setting lifecycle policies for old uploads
#
# 3. S3 Bucket Configuration:
#    - Enable versioning for rollback capability
#    - Set up CloudFront for CDN if needed
#    - Configure CORS if frontend is on different domain
#    - Set lifecycle rules to transition to cheaper storage (Glacier)
#
# 4. Example bucket policy to allow uploads:
#    {
#      "Version": "2012-10-17",
#      "Statement": [
#        {
#          "Effect": "Allow",
#          "Principal": {
#            "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:user/hostel-api"
#          },
#          "Action": [
#            "s3:PutObject",
#            "s3:DeleteObject",
#            "s3:GetObject"
#          ],
#          "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::hostel-production-storage/*"
#        }
#      ]
#    }
